           "w": "4/4",
           "items": [
            {
             "t": "text",
             "html": "<h2><span style=\"color: #217a86;\">SCHOOLS IN SAN CARLOS</span></h2>",
             "look": {
              "h1": {
               "c": "teal-700"
              },
              "b": {
               "f": "label",
               "w": "400",
               "c": "white",
               "s": 26
              }
             }
            },
            {
             "t": "text",
             "html": "<h2>Top Schools in California</h2>",
             "look": {
              "b": {
               "f": "heading",
               "w": "400",
               "c": "ink-500",
               "s": 50,
               "ps": 35
              },
              "h2": {
               "f": "heading",
               "s": 42
              }
             }
            },
            {
             "t": "text",
             "html": "<p>Public schools overseen by the San Carlos School District rank among the highest in the all of United States. Elementary and Middle Schools in San Carlos place within the top 5% in the state of California.</p>\n<p>On January 2023 the California Department of Education (CDE) came out with its list of distinguished elementary schools and every elementary school in San Carlos CA made the list. Of the 5,872 elementary schools in California, only 356 were selected (roughly 6%). Leading the group is White Oaks Elementary School which ranks at about #5 of all Californian Elementary Schools, while Central Middle School ranks #100 out of all Californian Middle Schools.</p>\n<p>The municipal public education system in San Carlos serves students from kindergarten through eighth grade across nine schools within our city.</p>\n<p>Older students travel to nearby Carlmont High School in Belmont or Sequoia High School in Redwood City to complete their secondary education, both of which are part of the Sequoia Union High School District.</p>"
            },
            {
             "t": "accordion",
             "items": [
              {
               "t": "toggle",
               "title": "Based on my address, what schools will my children go to?",
               "html": "<p>Click here to find out!  <strong><a href=\"https://locator.decisioninsite.com/?studyId=199008\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">San Carlos School Locator</a></strong></p>",
               "open": true
              },
              {
               "t": "toggle",
               "title": "Who can I contact for more information?",
               "html": "<p>You may contact the <strong><a href=\"https://www.scsdk8.org/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">San Carlos School District</a></strong></p>\n<p><strong>San Carlos School District</strong><br/>1200 Industrial Road, Unit 9<br/>San Carlos, CA 94070<br/>Phone: (650) 508-7333, Fax: (650) 508-7340</p>\n<p>To contact individual departments within the district office, you may refer to the <strong><a href=\"https://www.scsdk8.org/apps/pages/index.jsp?uREC_ID=1136262&amp;type=d&amp;pREC_ID=1394035\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">District Staff</a></strong> page.</p>",
               "open": false
              },
              {
               "t": "toggle",
               "title": "Where can I read the whole guide?",
               "html": "<p>Click here. <a href=\"https://www.scsdk8.org/apps/pages/School-Boundaries\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>San Carlos School Boundaries</strong></a></p>",
               "open": false
              }
             ]
            }
           ]
          }
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      {
       "w": "1/2",
       "items": [
        {
         "t": "image",
